# The push-decision golden: one oracle read by every implementation.
#
# Format: <code>|<attempt>|<write-failed>|<expected-outcome>
#
# code is the dispatcher exit code (0 success; 70 retryable; 71 terminal;
# 72 not-available; 73 unrecognised; anything else is an unknown code,
# handled conservatively). attempt is 1 (first) or 2 (the one retry).
# write-failed is 0|1 — consulted only when code is 0.
# expected ∈ write-once|retry|local-save|loud-terminal

0|1|0|write-once
0|1|1|loud-terminal
70|1|0|retry
70|2|0|local-save
71|1|0|loud-terminal
71|2|0|loud-terminal
72|1|0|local-save
73|1|0|local-save
0|2|0|write-once
99|1|0|loud-terminal
70|1|1|retry
71|1|1|loud-terminal
